# Data conversion between gibibyte and megabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between gibibyte and megabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1GiB to 1073.7418MB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5GiB yields 1610.6127MB; backward, converting 1MB to 0.0009GiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5MB yields 0.0013GiB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1GiB
print(forward_whole->to(MB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GiB
print(forward_fractional->to(MB))
backward_whole: int = 1MB
print(backward_whole->to(GiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MB
print(backward_fractional->to(GiB))

<<< stdout
1073.7418MB
1610.6127MB
0.0009GiB
0.0013GiB

<<< stderr
